{"name":"Wintergreen Dream","hex":"#56887d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wintergreen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any evergreen plant.","One of various not closely related evergreen plants, including:\nPlants in shrub genus Gaultheria, commonly known as wintergreen, especially:\nGaultheria procumbens, native to North America, having solitary white flowers and aromatic leaves (checkerberry or teaberry)\nGaultheria humifusa – alpine wintergreen\nGaultheria ovatifolia – western teaberry or Oregon spicy wintergreen\nChimaphila maculata – striped wintergreen, pipsissewa\nPlants in any of several other genera in the herbaceous family Ericaceae, including:\nGenus Pyrola, native to northern temperate and Arctic regions.\nGenus Orthilia\nGenus Moneses\nGenus Chimaphila (prince's pine, pipsissewa)\nSome species of the herbaceous genus Trientalis, in family Primulaceae (chickweed wintergreen)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wintergreen"},{"term":"dream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Imaginary events seen in the mind while sleeping.","A hope or wish."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To see imaginary events in one's mind while sleeping.","To hope, to wish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wintergreen","blocks":[{"text":"Wintergreen is a group of aromatic plants. The term wintergreen once commonly referred to plants that remain green throughout the winter. The term evergreen is now more commonly used for this characteristic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/FountainSpringsWintergreen.png/330px-FountainSpringsWintergreen.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wintergreen","wikidata":"Q1785217"},{"title":"Dream","blocks":[{"text":"A dream is a succession of images, dynamic scenes and situations, ideas, emotions, and sensations that usually occur involuntarily in the mind during certain stages of sleep. Humans generally spend more than two hours dreaming per night, and each dream lasts around 5–20 minutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg/330px-A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dream","wikidata":"Q36348"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Wintergreenleavesandberries.jpg/500px-Wintergreenleavesandberries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Wintergreenleavesandberries.jpg/1280px-Wintergreenleavesandberries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Wintergreenleavesandberries.jpg/500px-Wintergreenleavesandberries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wintergreen from Greeley, Pennsylvania; early December","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWintergreenleavesandberries.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/WintergreenEssentialOil.png/500px-WintergreenEssentialOil.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/WintergreenEssentialOil.png/500px-WintergreenEssentialOil.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wintergreen (Gaultheria procumbens) essential oil","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWintergreenEssentialOil.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Raja_Ravi_Varma%2C_Usha%27s_Dream_%28oleographic_print%29.jpg/500px-Raja_Ravi_Varma%2C_Usha%27s_Dream_%28oleographic_print%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm